---
description: Apply comprehensive React Native best practices for code structure, state, styling, and performance in `apps/frontend`.
globs: apps/frontend/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

General:
- Use TypeScript everywhere
- Prefer functional components
- Keep feature-based folders

Files:
- Name components with PascalCase
- Co-locate styles and tests
- Use module aliases for imports

Component Architecture:
- Smart components handle logic
- Dumb components display only
- Place displayName at bottom
- Return null if props missing
- Avoid default export
- One component per file
- Extract platform code with Platform.select

State Management:
- Delegate state to smart components
- Use hooks for async logic
- Clean up subscriptions on unmount
- Lift shared state up

Styling:
- Use StyleSheet.create
- Prefer flexbox layout
- Reuse platform style constants
- Keep styles near components
- Avoid global styles

Performance:
- Use FlatList for lists
- Memoize heavy components
- Use useCallback for handlers
- Lazy load screens
- Debounce expensive calls

Security:
- Validate and sanitize input
- Use HTTPS for APIs
- Securely store secrets

Testing:
- Unit test with Jest
- End-to-end test with Detox
- Keep tests near code

Tooling:
- Use VS Code with React Native Tools
- Lint and format with ESLint and Prettier
- Integrate CI/CD for builds
